      "extraction_method": "ARTICLE",
      "body_chars": 0,
      "body_sha256": null,
      "candidate": false,
      "decision": "NO_EVIDENCE",
      "reason": null,
      "evidence": {
        "DEMAND": [
          "If procurement strategies continue to prioritize carrying-cost reduction over operational continuity, they will remain structurally vulnerable to modern supply chain volatility.",
          "Strategic buffering begins with a foundational realization: Not all components on a bill of materials (BOM) carry equal risk, so they shouldn’t share the same procurement strategy."
        ],
        "CAPACITY_LEAD_TIME": [
          "For three decades, the gospel of just-in-time (JIT) inventory management went virtually unchallenged across high-tech manufacturing.",
          "Between volatile semiconductor node transitions, specialized memory module lead times stretching past 30 weeks, and persistent geopolitical friction along primary shipping lanes, pure JIT has transformed from a lean operations strategy into a single point of failure."
        ],
        "TIMING": [
          "When an electronics manufacturing line goes down, the costs extend far beyond delayed revenue, taking the form of:",
          "Qualifying a secondary source for these elements would take six to 12 months of engineering and regulatory re-validation."
        ]
      },
