    "c3ece031-d78c-48ea-97b6-8c5192544da9": {
      "id": "c3ece031-d78c-48ea-97b6-8c5192544da9",
      "title": "The High Cost of Legacy Tech in the Shipping Department",
      "url": "https://www.supplychainbrain.com/blogs/1-think-tank/post/44638-the-high-cost-of-legacy-tech-in-the-shipping-department",
      "source": "www.supplychainbrain.com",
      "collected_at": "2026-09-30T22:02:08.735988+00:00",
      "updated_at": "2026-09-30T22:02:08.735999+00:00",
      "fingerprint": "419b57594c3678ed87ff49bcd14aadb5cc678d5a241b305198b94506b92164c2",
      "attempts": 2,
      "checked_at": "2026-10-03T10:07:47.233751+00:00",
      "body_status": "UNAVAILABLE",
      "extraction_method": "ARTICLE",
      "body_chars": 0,
      "body_sha256": null,
      "candidate": false,
      "decision": "NO_EVIDENCE",
      "reason": null,
      "evidence": {
        "DEMAND": [
          "Across the decades, retailers have welcomed growing online order volumes, while successful e-commerce businesses have set themselves apart by recognizing the importance of adapting their fulfillment practices to meet the changing expectations of shoppers.",
          "Siloed desktop parcel shipping applications have evolved into integrated fulfillment platforms, streamlining and simplifying every stage of the order journey from the warehouse to the customer."
        ],
        "CAPACITY_LEAD_TIME": [
          "Some retailers are resistant to change, concerned about the impact of change latency on fulfillment output; others are simply lulled into complacency by the status quo, unable to see how legacy shipping platforms are increasing customer churn and stunting profits through inefficiencies, errors and cost creep.",
          "Plus, siloed legacy systems stifle an organization’s agility and limit its capacity to make data-driven decisions."
        ],
        "TIMING": [
          "Back in 1994, a 21-year-old college student changed history with the world’s first digitally secure credit card transaction (a Sting CD!) on his company’s online marketplace.",
          "By 2016, roughly eight in 10 Americans were online shoppers."
        ],
        "RELIEF": [
          "As the evolving e-commerce landscape continued to shape shipping operations, many businesses grew from a single warehouse to multiple distribution centers, added regional parcel carriers to control costs, and expanded into less-than-truckload (LTL) freight.",
          "Whether adding new carriers, expanding internationally, opening another warehouse, introducing scanner-based picking or supporting new retail customers, modern fulfillment platforms are designed to grow alongside the business rather than require another technology replacement a few years later."
        ]
      },
      "targets": [],
      "target_status": "UNRESOLVED",
